WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.838
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online English for Academic Purposes.

2
00:00:06.138 --> 00:00:09.513
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.813 --> 00:00:15.832
Unit seventeen: Seminar Discussion Skills. Today you will take part in an academic group discussion.

4
00:00:16.132 --> 00:00:18.900
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.867 --> 00:00:23.100
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:24.928
Contribute.

7
00:00:25.917 --> 00:00:28.114
Contribute means to add your ideas.

8
00:00:28.717 --> 00:00:30.449
Contribute to the discussion.

9
00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:33.737
Your turn. Say: Contribute.

10
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:37.497
Contribute.

11
00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.216
Interrupt.

12
00:00:40.217 --> 00:00:42.646
Interrupt means to stop someone speaking.

13
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:44.855
Do not interrupt rudely.

14
00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:47.940
Your turn. Say: Interrupt.

15
00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:51.569
Interrupt.

16
00:00:52.317 --> 00:00:53.225
Agree.

17
00:00:54.217 --> 00:00:56.379
Agree means to share the same view.

18
00:00:56.983 --> 00:00:58.286
I agree with you.

19
00:00:58.883 --> 00:01:01.733
Your turn. Say: Agree.

20
00:01:04.567 --> 00:01:05.475
Agree.

21
00:01:06.217 --> 00:01:07.241
Disagree.

22
00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:10.238
Disagree means to have a different view.

23
00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:12.455
I disagree politely.

24
00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:15.354
Your turn. Say: Disagree.

25
00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:19.224
Disagree.

26
00:01:19.983 --> 00:01:21.101
Clarify.

27
00:01:22.117 --> 00:01:24.000
Clarify means to make clear.

28
00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:26.163
Could you clarify that?

29
00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:29.635
Your turn. Say: Clarify.

30
00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:33.466
Clarify.

31
00:01:34.217 --> 00:01:35.229
Turn-taking.

32
00:01:36.217 --> 00:01:38.297
Turn-taking means speaking in order.

33
00:01:38.883 --> 00:01:40.465
Turn-taking is polite.

34
00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:43.865
Your turn. Say: Turn-taking.

35
00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:47.840
Turn-taking.

36
00:01:48.583 --> 00:01:49.550
Challenge.

37
00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:52.933
Challenge means to question an idea.

38
00:01:53.517 --> 00:01:55.470
Challenge ideas respectfully.

39
00:01:56.083 --> 00:01:58.631
Your turn. Say: Challenge.

40
00:02:01.467 --> 00:02:02.445
Challenge.

41
00:02:03.183 --> 00:02:04.359
Consensus.

42
00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:07.350
Consensus means general agreement.

43
00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:09.857
The group reached consensus.

44
00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:13.323
Your turn. Say: Consensus.

45
00:02:16.167 --> 00:02:17.481
Consensus.

46
00:02:18.267 --> 00:02:21.685
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:24.898
Visal, I am shy in seminars.

48
00:02:25.983 --> 00:02:34.824
Prepare one or two points before class. Then use phrases such as I would like to add or Building on what Sam said to join the discussion.

49
00:02:35.917 --> 00:02:37.719
How do I disagree politely?

50
00:02:38.817 --> 00:02:47.460
Say I see your point, but or I am not sure I agree because. Give a reason and avoid saying you are wrong.

51
00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:50.677
How do I ask for clarification?

52
00:02:51.783 --> 00:02:58.165
Say Could you explain what you mean by that? or Do you mean that? This shows that you listen and want to understand.

53
00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:00.870
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:01.717 --> 00:03:05.133
Grammar focus: Polite phrases for discussion.

55
00:03:05.433 --> 00:03:06.631
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:07.317 --> 00:03:10.953
I see your point, but I am not sure because the data are old.

57
00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:14.465
I would like to add that cost is also important.

58
00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:21.593
Use polite openers such as I see your point, but and I would like to add that. Always give a reason when you disagree.

59
00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:25.780
Be careful! Don't say: I am not agree with you.

60
00:03:27.733 --> 00:03:29.791
Say: I do not agree with you.

61
00:03:30.091 --> 00:03:31.522
Use do not agree.

62
00:03:32.333 --> 00:03:35.137
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:35.933 --> 00:03:37.352
A Group Discussion.

64
00:03:37.652 --> 00:03:40.256
The class discusses whether homework is useful.

65
00:03:41.267 --> 00:03:44.183
Lina prepares two points before the seminar.

66
00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.467
She builds on a classmate's idea politely.

67
00:03:48.467 --> 00:03:51.035
When she disagrees, she gives a clear reason.

68
00:03:52.033 --> 00:03:54.973
The group reaches consensus on a short homework plan.

69
00:03:56.067 --> 00:04:00.057
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:00.917 --> 00:04:02.800
To contribute is to add your blank.

71
00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:06.754
A, shoes. B, tickets. C, ideas.

72
00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.392
The answer is C: ideas.

73
00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:15.875
Turn-taking means speaking in blank.

74
00:04:16.175 --> 00:04:19.236
A, order. B, anger. C, secret.

75
00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:24.335
The answer is A: order.

76
00:04:25.483 --> 00:04:27.239
Consensus is general blank.

77
00:04:27.539 --> 00:04:31.018
A, delay. B, agreement. C, noise.

78
00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:36.961
The answer is B: agreement.

79
00:04:38.117 --> 00:04:40.093
Politely disagree with a blank.

80
00:04:40.393 --> 00:04:43.489
A, shout. B, joke. C, reason.

81
00:04:47.033 --> 00:04:49.207
The answer is C: reason.

82
00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:51.885
What did Lina prepare?

83
00:04:52.185 --> 00:04:56.106
A, two points. B, a song. C, a map.

84
00:04:59.667 --> 00:05:01.933
The answer is A: two points.

85
00:05:03.133 --> 00:05:06.459
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:07.317 --> 00:05:09.444
How do you join a seminar discussion?

87
00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:19.669
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:19.969 --> 00:05:31.006
I prepare one or two points before class. I use polite phrases to add ideas and I give reasons when I disagree. I also ask for clarification when I do not understand.

89
00:05:31.306 --> 00:05:33.097
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:33.983 --> 00:05:38.656
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and polite phrases for discussion.

91
00:05:38.956 --> 00:05:43.953
Today's value is respectful disagreement. Disagree politely and listen to others.

92
00:05:44.253 --> 00:05:46.743
See you in Unit eighteen. Goodbye!

93
00:05:47.043 --> 00:05:50.137
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

